{
  "_what": "The places a person posts to, one row per place: which kind of connection reaches the account (connection_vendor: a connection record of that vendor, `service_connection:<vendor>` or `service_connection:<vendor>:<name>`), how a publisher is filled from it (options and account: {held: field} is a value held in the person's vault, read only as the request leaves, and {held: field, sign} a value made from it then (read-data/send-a-post.mjs signers: jwt-hs256 with claims and seconds); {plain: field} is a readable field of their connection record; {value} is fixed), which hosts a held value may go to, how a post's file reaches the place (media_from: stream, its bytes streamed to the place; whole, its bytes handed as one piece to a place whose uploader takes a file only so; address, a share of it the place fetches), the settings sent unless the post names its own (default_settings), and what the place takes (format: read by read-data/post-ready.mjs), and which tool row sends to it (send_tool, run at a post's time by tool:send-each-post-at-its-time). Read by read-data/posts.mjs. A place reached by a plain JSON API takes adapter requests and writes its requests in its options (read-data/publisher-requests.mjs). A new place is a row; nothing in the code names a place.",
